com/users/nickderobertis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickderobertis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1c80fdcc9409dad6aadbe37542b6917744b5a4c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/commits/1c80fdcc9409dad6aadbe37542b6917744b5a4c5","html_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/commit/1c80fdcc9409dad6aadbe37542b6917744b5a4c5"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"9a03efe17561f61c3dacb91a7c0f29992a866565","filename":".gitattributes","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changes":4,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.gitattributes","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.gitattributes","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.gitattributes?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -9,3 +9,7 @@\n # The vendored screenshot font is binary; `text=auto` above detects that, and this says so\n # outright so no future eol rule can be read as reaching it.\n *.ttf -text\n+\n+# Recorded GitHub responses, byte for byte as `gh api --include` printed them: their header\n+# lines end in CRLF, which is what the release-tail replay serves back.\n+.github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/recordings/*.http -text"},{"sha":"a0b5f8558f2af49437ba427c2884d0dbe9c74f3b","filename":".github/README.md","status":"modified","additions":10,"deletions":5,"changes":15,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2FREADME.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2FREADME.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2FREADME.md?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -15,12 +15,17 @@ requiring Mac. Non-PR automatic events never require Mac. A same-repository `rel\n branch and semantic version/changelog-only diff authorize omission; an author's identity\n or a title does not. The classifier prints JSON and writes the corresponding fields to\n `GITHUB_OUTPUT` when supplied. Its exit codes are 0 for a decision and 1 for invalid\n-invocation or failed output IO; a failed classifier cannot satisfy either required carrier.\n+invocation or failed output IO. `lint` runs it on this repository's `release-plz-` branch,\n+where `test-macos` is skipped, and fails unless it authorizes the omission.\n \n-`macos-result.mjs NEEDS_JSON` exits 0 only for successful required work or a successful\n-classification authorizing skipped work; explicit manual diagnostics require successful\n-work. It exits 1 for malformed inputs or failed/cancelled/missing prerequisites, prints\n-errors to stderr, and distinguishes omission from executed proof in stdout.\n+The root `budgets.yaml`'s seven `release-tail` budgets are checked by `publish`'s last step;\n+`policy/tests/release-tail.test.mjs` runs that step and the install step before it as\n+release.yml writes them, over GitHub responses recorded from this repository under\n+`policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/` (its README says how they were taken and how to reconcile\n+them). It is `github-workflow-policy:release-tail`, a target of its own in the project no crate\n+edit selects, because it installs from npm. `tests/ci-events.test.mjs` holds which workflows\n+and jobs run on a pull request and on the release commit, and `tests/gate-time.test.mjs` the\n+timing wrapper `just gate` runs inside; those two are `github-workflows:budget-journeys`.\n \n `policy/macos-budget.mjs --metric jobs-per-run|runs-per-change --telemetry PATH` exits 0 after\n validating and reporting current telemetry, and 1 for invalid invocation, missing/stale"},{"sha":"a72912da8012c0b5071363a02d88f5786099ddfa","filename":".github/event-classes.json","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":15,"changes":16,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fevent-classes.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fevent-classes.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fevent-classes.json?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -9,19 +9,5 @@\n   { \"id\": \"downstream\", \"event\": \"workflow_run\", \"action\": \"completed\" },\n   { \"id\": \"dispatch\", \"event\": \"repository_dispatch\", \"action\": \"release-smoke\" },\n   { \"id\": \"schedule\", \"event\": \"schedule\" },\n-  {\n-    \"id\": \"manual-default\",\n-    \"event\": \"workflow_dispatch\",\n-    \"inputs\": { \"macos\": false, \"distribution\": false }\n-  },\n-  {\n-    \"id\": \"manual-opt-in\",\n-    \"event\": \"workflow_dispatch\",\n-    \"inputs\": { \"macos\": true, \"distribution\": false }\n-  },\n-  {\n-    \"id\": \"manual-distribution\",\n-    \"event\": \"workflow_dispatch\",\n-    \"inputs\": { \"macos\": false, \"distribution\": true }\n-  }\n+  { \"id\": \"manual-default\", \"event\": \"workflow_dispatch\" }\n ]"},{"sha":"0d0b9c6f9861964d705c3806fc7e693ce37fe7b8","filename":".github/linear-documents-policy/policy.test.mjs","status":"modified","additions":11,"deletions":10,"changes":21,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Flinear-documents-policy%2Fpolicy.test.mjs","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Flinear-documents-policy%2Fpolicy.test.mjs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Flinear-documents-policy%2Fpolicy.test.mjs?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -8,21 +8,19 @@ import { read, workflows } from \"../workflow-graph.mjs\";\n \n // The service owns the queue. Reconcile its actual declarations instead of simulating\n // a second scheduler whose behavior could disagree with Actions.\n-test(\"ordinary, daily and explicit initialization retain three pending CI writers\", () => {\n+test(\"pull-request, daily and explicit initialization retain every pending CI writer\", () => {\n   const definitions = workflows();\n   const ci = definitions[\"ci.yml\"];\n   const creation = definitions[\"linear-documents.yml\"];\n   assert.equal(ci.concurrency, undefined, \"outer cancellation must not cancel pending checks\");\n-  // A push's credentials are on check's Linux leg; a pull request's on test-linux.\n-  const ordinary = ci.jobs.check.concurrency;\n-  assert.match(ordinary.group, /'linear-live-documents'/);\n+  // The credentials are on test-linux alone; no job writes the standing set on a push.\n   const pullRequest = ci.jobs[\"test-linux\"].concurrency;\n   assert.equal(pullRequest.group, \"linear-live-documents\");\n   const daily = creation.jobs.documents.concurrency;\n   assert.equal(daily.group, \"linear-live-documents\");\n-  // Three simultaneous pending writers must all reach the service's 100-waiter queue;\n-  // the default single pending setting would silently replace two required checks.\n-  for (const declaration of [ordinary, pullRequest, daily, daily]) {\n+  // Simultaneous pending writers must all reach the service's 100-waiter queue; the\n+  // default single pending setting would silently replace a pending required check.\n+  for (const declaration of [pullRequest, pullRequest, daily, daily]) {\n     assert.equal(declaration[\"cancel-in-progress\"], false);\n     assert.equal(declaration.queue, \"max\");\n   }\n@@ -71,11 +69,14 @@ test(\"only the daily schedule creates fresh documents and manual dispatch initia\n   }\n   const credentialed = (job) =>\n     definitions[\"ci.yml\"].jobs[job].steps.filter((step) => step.env?.LINEAR_API_KEY);\n-  const ordinarySteps = [...credentialed(\"check\"), ...credentialed(\"test-linux\")];\n-  assert.ok(credentialed(\"test-linux\").length > 0, \"test-linux carries a pull request's session\");\n+  // test-linux is the one job any credential reaches.\n+  for (const job of Object.keys(definitions[\"ci.yml\"].jobs).filter((id) => id !== \"test-linux\"))\n+    assert.deepEqual(credentialed(job), [], `${job} is handed LINEAR_API_KEY`);\n+  const ordinarySteps = credentialed(\"test-linux\");\n+  assert.ok(ordinarySteps.length > 0, \"test-linux carries a pull request's session\");\n   for (const step of ordinarySteps) {\n     assert.equal(step.env.ONETASKGRAPH_LINEAR_DOCUMENT_MODE, \"ordinary\");\n-    assert.match(step.run, /^just ((check|gate)-generated|ci-test-linux)$/);\n+    assert.equal(step.run, \"just ci-test-linux\");\n   }\n });\n "},{"sha":"bbeef30f543f6ac2d9d62bc644325b4c895f86ac","filename":".github/macos-result.mjs","status":"removed","additions":0,"deletions":32,"changes":32,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/1416a41df9a19e1c66b29c84a35631080813f351/.github%2Fmacos-result.mjs","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/1416a41df9a19e1c66b29c84a35631080813f351/.github%2Fmacos-result.mjs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fmacos-result.mjs?ref=1416a41df9a19e1c66b29c84a35631080813f351","patch":"@@ -1,32 +0,0 @@\n-import { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n-\n-// Job outcomes are the GitHub boundary. Missing or cancelled proofs never become green.\n-try {\n-  if (process.argv.slice(2).length !== 1)\n-    throw Error(\n-      \"usage: macos-result.mjs NEEDS_JSON; next: pass one readable job-outcome JSON file\",\n-    );\n-  const needs = JSON.parse(readFileSync(process.argv[2], \"utf8\"));\n-  if (needs[\"macos-lanes\"]?.result !== \"success\")\n-    throw Error(\"macOS classification failed or is missing\");\n-  const diagnostic = needs[\"macos-lanes\"].outputs?.diagnostic;\n-  if (diagnostic !== undefined && ![\"true\", \"false\"].includes(diagnostic))\n-    throw Error(\"Malformed macOS diagnostic output\");\n-  const required =\n-    needs[\"macos-lanes\"].outputs?.diagnostic === \"true\"\n-      ? \"true\"\n-      : needs[\"macos-lanes\"].outputs?.macosRequired;\n-  // The proof is the pull request's `test-macos`, or the manual diagnostic's `macos`.\n-  const result = (diagnostic === \"true\" ? needs.macos : needs[\"test-macos\"])?.result;\n-  if (required === \"true\" && result === \"success\")\n-    console.log(\"The combined macOS check and install proofs passed.\");\n-  else if (required === \"false\" && result === \"skipped\") {\n-    const reason = needs[\"macos-lanes\"].outputs.reason;\n-    if (typeof reason !== \"string\" || !reason.trim() || /[\\r\\n]/.test(reason))\n-      throw Error(\"Missing or malformed authorized omission reason\");\n-    console.log(`macOS omitted: ${reason}`);\n-  } else throw Error(`Required macOS work did not succeed: required=${required}, result=${result}`);\n-} catch (error) {\n-  console.error(error.message);\n-  process.exitCode = 1;\n-}"},{"sha":"7063255aeda316f99fa9e42ce1cbb9df242d4225","filename":".github/policy/project.json","status":"modified","additions":23,"deletions":2,"changes":25,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Fproject.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Fproject.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Fproject.json?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -34,6 +34,17 @@\n       \"{workspaceRoot}/scripts/check-real-release-preparation.sh\",\n       \"{workspaceRoot}/scripts/check-npm-publish.sh\",\n       \"{workspaceRoot}/scripts/check-fixture-discrimination.sh\"\n+    ],\n+    \"releaseTail\": [\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/.github/workflows/release.yml\",\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/.github/workflows/rust-cache-warm.yml\",\n+      \"{projectRoot}/tests/release-tail.test.mjs\",\n+      \"{projectRoot}/tests/fixtures/release-tail/**/*\",\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/.github/package.json\",\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/.github/bun.lock\",\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/budgets.yaml\",\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/package.json\",\n+      \"{workspaceRoot}/scripts/actions-budget-figures.sh\"\n     ]\n   },\n   \"targets\": {\n@@ -61,14 +72,14 @@\n       \"executor\": \"nx:run-commands\",\n       \"dependsOn\": [\"bootstrap\"],\n       \"options\": {\n-        \"command\": \"node --test .github/policy/tests/boundaries.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/inventory.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/policy-carriers.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/policy-routing.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/policy.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/release-shortcut.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/reusable.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/rust-cache-warm.test.mjs\"\n+        \"command\": \"node --test .github/policy/tests/boundaries.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/inventory.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/policy-routing.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/policy.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/release-shortcut.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/reusable.test.mjs .github/policy/tests/rust-cache-warm.test.mjs\"\n       },\n       \"cache\": false,\n       \"outputs\": [\"{workspaceRoot}/.github/.telemetry/macos-policy.json\"]\n     },\n     \"test\": {\n       \"executor\": \"nx:noop\",\n-      \"dependsOn\": [\"policy-tests\", \"rust-cache-action\"],\n+      \"dependsOn\": [\"policy-tests\", \"rust-cache-action\", \"release-tail\"],\n       \"cache\": false\n     },\n     \"budgets\": {\n@@ -91,6 +102,16 @@\n       },\n       \"cache\": false,\n       \"//\": \"The one policy journey that runs the real rust-cache action, which also runs on the Windows and macOS runners; test-windows and test-macos run this target alone, and test-linux runs it with the rest of `test`.\"\n+    },\n+    \"release-tail\": {\n+      \"executor\": \"nx:run-commands\",\n+      \"dependsOn\": [\"bootstrap\"],\n+      \"options\": {\n+        \"command\": \"node --test .github/policy/tests/release-tail.test.mjs\"\n+      },\n+      \"inputs\": [\"releaseTail\"],\n+      \"cache\": true,\n+      \"//\": \"publish's release tail: its install step and its last step run as release.yml writes them over GitHub answers recorded from this repository (tests/fixtures/release-tail/). Here, in the project no crate or SDK edit selects, and a target of its own keyed on its reads alone, because it installs onevcs and onebudgetspec from npm.\"\n     }\n   }\n }"},{"sha":"65b09076c3965003bb1c246d9d9e9c7014e138af","filename":".github/policy/tests/boundaries.test.mjs","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":39,"changes":42,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Fboundaries.test.mjs","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Fboundaries.test.mjs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Fboundaries.test.mjs?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -279,13 +279,12 @@ test(\"local Bun parser rejects unsupported CLI arguments at its real entrypoint\"\n   assert.equal(JSON.parse(accepted.stdout).workspaces[\"sdks/typescript\"].name, \"@onetaskgraph/sdk\");\n });\n \n-test(\"classifier and carriers enforce invocation and actual filesystem IO failure contracts\", () => {\n+test(\"the classifier enforces invocation and actual filesystem IO failure contracts\", () => {\n   const scratch = mkdtempSync(\n     join(process.env.ONEPIPELINE_NODE_SCRATCH_DIR || tmpdir(), \"cli-io-\"),\n   );\n   try {\n     const classifier = fileURLToPath(new URL(\"../../macos-policy.mjs\", import.meta.url));\n-    const carrier = fileURLToPath(new URL(\"../../macos-result.mjs\", import.meta.url));\n     const event = join(scratch, \"event.json\");\n     writeFileSync(event, JSON.stringify({ event_name: \"push\" }));\n     for (const args of [[], [\"other\"], [\"classify\", \"--unknown\", event]])\n@@ -302,41 +301,6 @@ test(\"classifier and carriers enforce invocation and actual filesystem IO failur\n       },\n     );\n     assert.notEqual(outputFailure.status, 0);\n-    const needs = join(scratch, \"needs.json\");\n-    for (const path of [join(scratch, \"missing.json\"), scratch])\n-      assert.notEqual(spawnSync(process.execPath, [carrier, path], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).status, 0);\n-    writeFileSync(needs, \"{bad\");\n-    assert.notEqual(spawnSync(process.execPath, [carrier, needs], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).status, 0);\n-    for (const reason of [undefined, null, {}, \"\", \" \\n\"]) {\n-      writeFileSync(\n-        needs,\n-        JSON.stringify({\n-          \"macos-lanes\": { result: \"success\", outputs: { macosRequired: \"false\", reason } },\n-          macos: { result: \"skipped\" },\n-          \"test-macos\": { result: \"skipped\" },\n-        }),\n-      );\n-      assert.notEqual(\n-        spawnSync(process.execPath, [carrier, needs], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).status,\n-        0,\n-      );\n-    }\n-    writeFileSync(\n-      needs,\n-      JSON.stringify({\n-        \"macos-lanes\": {\n-          result: \"success\",\n-          outputs: { macosRequired: \"false\", reason: \"authorized semantic release\" },\n-        },\n-        macos: { result: \"skipped\" },\n-        \"test-macos\": { result: \"skipped\" },\n-      }),\n-    );\n-    assert.notEqual(\n-      spawnSync(process.execPath, [carrier, needs, \"extra\"], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).status,\n-      0,\n-    );\n-    assert.equal(spawnSync(process.execPath, [carrier, needs], { encoding: \"utf8\" }).status, 0);\n   } finally {\n     rmSync(scratch, { recursive: true, force: true });\n   }\n@@ -391,10 +355,10 @@ test(\"event workload rejects new workflow triggers, actions and diagnostic input\n       workflow.on.pull_request = { types: [\"edited\"] };\n     },\n     (workflow) => {\n-      workflow.on.workflow_dispatch.inputs.extra = { type: \"boolean\", default: false };\n+      workflow.on.workflow_dispatch = { inputs: { extra: { type: \"boolean\", default: false } } };\n     },\n     (workflow) => {\n-      workflow.on.workflow_dispatch.inputs.macos.type = \"string\";\n+      workflow.on.workflow_dispatch = { inputs: { macos: { type: \"string\" } } };\n     },\n   ]) {\n     const definitions = workflows();"},{"sha":"824f0c6d3882464b394bef11b2564d1775e99c42","filename":".github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/README.md","status":"added","additions":21,"deletions":0,"changes":21,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2FREADME.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2FREADME.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2FREADME.md?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+# Recorded GitHub responses for the release tail\n+\n+`../../release-tail.test.mjs` replays these through `ONEVCS_GH`, onevcs's seam for replaying\n+recorded responses, while it runs `publish`'s last step as release.yml writes it. Every file under\n+`recordings/` is a real GitHub REST response in onevcs's envelope — `{\"request\", \"status\",\n+\"headers\", \"body\"}` — recorded read-only from this repository with\n+`gh api --include --method GET <path>` on 2026-10-31, byte for byte as gh printed it. Its\n+`<name>.source.json` sidecar names the API path and the release, pull request or run it was\n+fetched for.\n+\n+The release is v0.12.13 (commit 3b6b228f): its own three reads, the runs at its commit and at\n+each of its four pull requests' heads, and the jobs of every run the figures select. One more is\n+the releases listing answered 401 under an invalid token, the error status the tail must exit\n+non-zero on. Nothing is hand-written or edited: the one change any response is served with — the\n+`publish` job of the Release run served in progress, because the tail runs inside it — is the\n+test's, applied when it serves, and named by that recording's sidecar under\n+`served_in_progress`.\n+\n+`reconcile.mjs` re-fetches every path and diffs it against its recording, ignoring only what\n+GitHub rewrites (the date, etag, last-modified, rate-limit and request-id headers, and `download_count` and\n+`updated_at`). It reaches GitHub, so it runs by hand and never in a gate."},{"sha":"8da6a1d23ad60a3714def8df7d7d14b0ce1d7569","filename":".github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/reconcile.mjs","status":"added","additions":98,"deletions":0,"changes":98,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Freconcile.mjs","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Freconcile.mjs","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Freconcile.mjs?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@\n+// Re-fetch every recording under recordings/ from GitHub, read-only, and diff it against the\n+// committed fixture. It runs by hand, never in a gate — it reaches GitHub, and what GitHub answers\n+// moves — and says, for each recording, whether GitHub still answers what was recorded:\n+//\n+//   node .github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/reconcile.mjs\n+//\n+// Needs `gh` signed in with read access to this repository. The recorded 401 is re-fetched under\n+// an invalid token, as it was recorded. Ignored, and only these, because GitHub rewrites them on\n+// every answer or with no change to the record: the response's date, etag, last-modified,\n+// rate-limit and request-id headers, and the `download_count` and `updated_at` fields in a body. Exit 0 when\n+// every recording matches, 1 naming each that does not, and 2 when a read cannot be made at all.\n+import { spawnSync } from \"node:child_process\";\n+import { readdirSync, readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\n+\n+const RECORDINGS = new URL(\"./recordings/\", import.meta.url);\n+const IGNORED_HEADERS = /^(date|etag|last-modified|x-ratelimit-.*|x-github-request-id)$/;\n+const IGNORED_FIELDS = new Set([\"download_count\", \"updated_at\"]);\n+const INVALID_TOKEN = \"ghp_invalidreplaytoken000000000000000000000\";\n+\n+// `gh api --include` output: the status line, the headers, a blank line and the body.\n+function parse(text, what) {\n+  const split = text.indexOf(\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\");\n+  if (split === -1) throw Error(`${what} holds no response`);\n+  const [statusLine, ...headerLines] = text.slice(0, split).split(/\\r?\\n/);\n+  const status = statusLine.match(/^HTTP\\/[0-9.]+ ([1-5][0-9]{2})(?: |$)/)?.[1];\n+  if (!status) throw Error(`${what} starts with no HTTP status line: ${statusLine.slice(0, 80)}`);\n+  const headers = {};\n+  for (const line of headerLines) {\n+    const at = line.indexOf(\": \");\n+    if (at > 0) headers[line.slice(0, at).toLowerCase()] = line.slice(at + 2);\n+  }\n+  return {\n+    status: Number(status),\n+    headers,\n+    body: JSON.parse(text.slice(split + 4)),\n+  };\n+}\n+\n+function fetch(path, invalid) {\n+  const ran = spawnSync(\"gh\", [\"api\", \"--include\", \"--method\", \"GET\", path], {\n+    encoding: \"utf8\",\n+    maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024,\n+    env: invalid ? { ...process.env, GH_TOKEN: INVALID_TOKEN } : process.env,\n+  });\n+  if (ran.error) throw ran.error;\n+  return parse(ran.stdout, `gh's answer for ${path} (${ran.stderr.trim()})`);\n+}\n+\n+function differences(recorded, fetched, at = \"body\") {\n+  if (\n+    recorded === null ||\n+    fetched === null ||\n+    typeof recorded !== \"object\" ||\n+    typeof fetched !== \"object\"\n+  )\n+    return JSON.stringify(recorded) === JSON.stringify(fetched) ? [] : [at];\n+  if (Array.isArray(recorded) !== Array.isArray(fetched)) return [at];\n+  const keys = new Set([...Object.keys(recorded), ...Object.keys(fetched)]);\n+  return [...keys]\n+    .filter((key) => !IGNORED_FIELDS.has(key))\n+    .flatMap((key) => differences(recorded[key], fetched[key], `${at}.${key}`));\n+}\n+\n+let mismatched = 0;\n+try {\n+  for (const name of readdirSync(RECORDINGS).filter((n) => n.endsWith(\".http\"))) {\n+    const recorded = parse(readFileSync(new URL(name, RECORDINGS), \"utf8\"), name);\n+    const { path } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(new URL(`${name}.source.json`, RECORDINGS), \"utf8\"));\n+    const fetched = fetch(path, recorded.status !== 200);\n+    const found = [\n+      ...(recorded.status === fetched.status\n+        ? []\n+        : [`status ${recorded.status} is now ${fetched.status}`]),\n+      ...Object.keys(recorded.headers)\n+        .filter((header) => !IGNORED_HEADERS.test(header))\n+        .filter((header) => recorded.headers[header] !== fetched.headers[header])\n+        .map((header) => `header ${header}`),\n+      ...differences(recorded.body, fetched.body),\n+    ];\n+    if (found.length) {\n+      mismatched++;\n+      console.error(\n+        `${name}: GitHub now answers otherwise at ${found.slice(0, 20).join(\", \")}${found.length > 20 ? \", …\" : \"\"}`,\n+      );\n+    }\n+  }\n+} catch (error) {\n+  console.error(\n+    `reconcile: ${error.message}; next: sign gh in with read access to this repository (gh auth status) and re-run`,\n+  );\n+  process.exit(2);\n+}\n+if (mismatched) {\n+  console.error(\n+    `${mismatched} recording(s) no longer match GitHub. Re-record them read-only with \\`gh api --include --method GET <path> > <name>.http\\` and re-run .github/policy/tests/release-tail.test.mjs.`,\n+  );\n+  process.exitCode = 1;\n+}"},{"sha":"eeec111a89ca8e7c9032a09de2cc46fe75464bab","filename":".github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/recordings/compare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http","status":"added","additions":31,"deletions":0,"changes":31,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fcompare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fcompare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fcompare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418"},{"sha":"8ab45ad194a9bde2e96dc010d3e8a83be69c6d01","filename":".github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/recordings/compare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http.source.json","status":"added","additions":14,"deletions":0,"changes":14,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fcompare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http.source.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fcompare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http.source.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fcompare-v0.12.12-v0.12.13.http.source.json?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+{\n+  \"path\": \"repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/compare/v0.12.12...v0.12.13?per_page=100\",\n+  \"fetched_from\": {\n+    \"release\": \"v0.12.13\",\n+    \"read\": \"the comparison with the previous release\"\n+  },\n+  \"repository\": \"nickderobertis/onetaskgraph\",\n+  \"recorded\": {\n+    \"at\": \"Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:52:31 GMT\",\n+    \"with\": \"gh api --include --method GET 'repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/compare/v0.12.12...v0.12.13?per_page=100'\",\n+    \"read_only\": true,\n+    \"as\": \"exactly what gh printed: the status line, every response header and the body, unedited\"\n+  }\n+}"},{"sha":"33e9d04ba899de68ef0473057f8bd5baec5d6b46","filename":".github/policy/tests/fixtures/release-tail/recordings/jobs-of-pr-3821-run-40990600745.http","status":"added","additions":29,"deletions":0,"changes":29,"blob_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/blob/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fjobs-of-pr-3821-run-40990600745.http","raw_url":"https://github.com/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/raw/c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fjobs-of-pr-3821-run-40990600745.http","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nickderobertis/onetaskgraph/contents/.github%2Fpolicy%2Ftests%2Ffixtures%2Frelease-tail%2Frecordings%2Fjobs-of-pr-3821-run-40990600745.http?ref=c6adfa0d0fa7eaa7bc4f3588364d003fd893f418","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+HTTP/2.0 200 OK\n+Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *\r\n+Access-Control-Expose-Headers: ETag, Link, Location, Retry-After, X-GitHub-OTP, X-RateLimit-Limit, X-RateLimit-Remaining, X-RateLimit-Used, X-RateLimit-Resource, X-RateLimit-Reset, X-OAuth-Scopes, X-Accepted-OAuth-Scopes, X-Poll-Interval, X-GitHub-Media-Type, X-GitHub-SSO, X-GitHub-Request-Id, Deprecation, Sunset, Warning\r\n+Cache-Control: private, max-age=60, s-maxage=60\r\n+Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'\r\n+Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\r\n+Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:52:42 GMT\r\n+Etag: W/\"6223fa2df1926a7549cbeff08e8b54b1f521145db82c21cc2b8cba2a838051f5\"\r\n+Referrer-Policy: origin-when-cross-origin, strict-origin-when-cross-origin\r\n+Server: github.com\r\n+Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubdomains; preload\r\n+Vary: Accept, Authorization, Cookie, X-GitHub-OTP,Accept-Encoding, Accept, X-Requested-With\r\n+X-Accepted-Oauth-Scopes: \r\n+X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\r\n+X-Frame-Options: deny\r\n+X-Github-Api-Version-Selected: 2022-11-28\r\n+X-Github-Edge-Region: iad\r\n+X-Github-Media-Type: github.v3; format=json\r\n+X-Github-Request-Id: 6833:2BE60:5569D3:11CBD92:6AE60ECA\r\n+X-Oauth-Client-Id: 178c6fc778ccc68e1